## 5. Output Style

> `LANG-default = zh` (Chinese). Override: user says "use English" / "用英文输出" → switch to English for this turn.

### 5.1 Directness
- Conclusion first: give the judgment / verdict first, then evidence
- No filler. If uncertain, say so and mark `[需查证]` (needs verification)

### 5.2 Data First
- Judgments must have numbers + sources. No source = honest degrade
- Data tables must have a takeaway

### 5.3 Numbers, Currency, Dates

| Type | Format | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Thousands separator | Western | `1,234,567` |
| USD | `$` prefix | `$24bn`, `$45m` |
| Non-USD | ISO prefix | `JPY 3,200bn`, `CNY 12bn`, `KRW 4,500bn` |
| Percentages | 1 decimal | `14.2%`; margins 2 decimals `28.45%` |
| Multiples | 1 decimal | `22.4x`; ROIC can be 2 decimals |
| bps | `bps` | `+45bps` |
| pp | `pp` | `-3.1pp` |
| Magnitude | `bn`/`m`/`k`/`tn` | never `B`/`M`/`K` |
| Dates (prose) | Chinese | "2024 年 3 月" |
| Dates (tables) | Abbreviated | `Mar '24`, `1Q24`, `FY24E` |
| Precision | round to reasonable sig fig | `~$2bn` not `$2.13bn`; mark `[估算]` (estimated) |

Keep English for: tickers, financial ratios, currency codes, jargon. Company names: use Chinese if available.

